course: dictionary
lesson: 15781
title: Typically: what usually happens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Typically is a word that tells you what usually happens. It describes a pattern, not something that happens every single time. «It typically rains in April» means rain is common in April, but not every day.
explain: Look at the words around typically for clues. Words like usually, most, about or normally tell you it is a general rule. «A typical spider has eight legs» means most spiders have eight legs, so the word is pointing to the usual case.
explain: Typically can also sound a bit fed-up. «Typically, the bus was late again.» Here it means as you would expect, something annoying happened again. Read the rest of the sentence to tell which meaning you have.
fact: Typically means usually, in the way that something normally happens.
fact: «Typically» can also mean very like a certain person or thing, as in «a typically British breakfast».
fact: «Typically, the bus was late again» means as you would expect, and it is often said when something annoying happens.
fact: Phrases such as «typically between» and «typically late» show a general pattern, not an exact amount.
fact: In science and maths, «typically» means usually, in most cases but not all.
exercise: «It typically rains in April.» What does typically mean here? | Very loudly | Only once | Never | *Usually
exercise: «Typically, the bus was late again.» What does the word suggest? | Nobody was waiting for the bus | *As you would expect, something annoying happened | The bus was early for once
exercise: «She wore a typically British raincoat.» What does typically mean here? | Not at all | Only on Sundays | Very quickly | *In a way that is very like a British raincoat
test: «Typically, there are about 20 children in a class.» What does typically show? | A rule that is never broken | A number chosen by the teacher | An exact number that never changes | *A general pattern, usually but not always
test: Sam says «typically» always means never. Is he right? | Yes, it means never | No, it means very fast | *No, it means usually | Yes, it means always
exam: Which sentence uses typically to mean as you would expect, in an annoying way? | *«Typically, it rained on sports day.» | «It typically snows in January.» | «A typical spider has eight legs.» | «Dad typically makes pancakes on Sundays.»
